From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer builds chamfers
 whose distance equals its face and chamfers whose cuts meet or cross

CANDIDATE, authored on the branch fix/fillet-comb-chamfer, no PR. Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3300. Applies after 0060; shares its
construction and its helpers (copied, because 0060's are file-local).

BRepFilletAPI_MakeChamfer answers IsDone() == false when a distance equals the face it is measured
on (4 on a 4 mm wide top face), when two chamfers on opposite edges have distances that sum to the
face width (2 and 2 on 4 mm), and when they sum to more (the cuts cross). The fillet analogues are
OCCT#1177 and patches 0059 and 0060. After Compute() has failed, Build now:

 - builds each contour on its own, by the same builder, or for one straight edge between two planar
   rectangles at a right angle by cutting the shape with the half-space on the corner side of the cut
   line (a distance equal to its face ends the cut on the far edge); and
 - for contours that share no vertex, intersects (BRepAlgoAPI_Common) the results.

Every result must be one valid closed solid, must remove no less than the largest and no more than the
sum of what each contour removes, and the cut must remove exactly its section area times the edge
length. Otherwise the failure stands. Contours that share a vertex (frames, adjacent edges) still fail
as before.

A distance that RUNS PAST its face is a design choice nobody has made, so three readings are compiled
behind BRepFilletAPI_CHAMFER_RUNOUT: 0 declines (the default, the previous behaviour), 1 is the pivot
reading (the cut passes through the far edge and keeps the distance that fits), 2 is the half-space
reading (the plane through the two distances, extended and clipped by the solid).

ChFi3d_Builder gains the inline accessor FirstFaceOf(), the face on whose side the first distance of
a contour is measured (the map it reads already exists).

Measured on a 4 x 10 x 6 box (Scripts/repro/fillet-comb/): 42 chamfer cases, single, two-distance,
distance-angle, both edges, one after the other. Pinned kernel.6: 17 valid, 25 declined. With this
patch and reading 0: 28 valid and matching an independent sketch-and-extrude reference, 14 declined
(exactly the cases where the two readings differ). Reading 1: all 42 match the pivot reference.
Reading 2: all 42 match the half-space reference.

---
